    "answer": "Now I have a thorough understanding of the codebase. Let me frame the task and propose solution options.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task is to enrich the **flag reason** string with the **verify signature** \u2014 the compact, identifying summary of a failed verification (check status, tree hash, exit code, and/or failure reason). Currently, when the Verify gate (stage 10) or Fix-verify loop (stage 11) flags a task, the `reason` passed to `FlagAsync` is generic:\n\n- `\"verify failed\"` or `\"new test failures: {newFailures}\"` (stage 10, fix-verify disabled \u2014 `RelayDriver.cs:257-258`)\n- `\"verify failed after N fix-verify attempts\"` (stage 11 loop exhausted \u2014 `VerifyFix.cs:220-221`)\n\nThese reasons are written as the first line of the `NEEDS-REVIEW` file and later parsed by `FailedRunContextReader.Read` into `FailedRunContext.FlagReason`. The `FixTaskAuthorRunner` then includes this `FlagReason` in the prompt sent to the fix-task authoring subagent.\n\nHowever, the verify *signature* \u2014 the concrete `check` (red), the `treeHash` (working-tree fingerprint), the test `exitCode`, and the extracted failure `reason` \u2014 are all available at the flagging call site (they were just published in the `verify_result` event, see `VerifyObservability.cs:39-55`) but are **not** carried in the flag reason string. The subagent can only find them by separately scanning the `VerifyOutputs` list or the full verify-output artifact, which is less direct and more brittle.\n\n**Goal:** Include the verify signature in the flag reason so it flows through the `NEEDS-REVIEW` \u2192 `FailedRunContext.FlagReason` \u2192 `FixTaskAuthorRunner.BuildPrompt` pipeline without extra parsing steps.\n\n---\n\n## Solution options\n\n### Option A \u2014 Embed a compact verify signature in the FlagReason string\n\nModify the three call sites that flag with a verify-related reason to include a structured suffix like `[check:red treeHash:<hash>]`:\n\n1. `RelayDriver.cs:257-258` \u2014 stage 10 flag: change `\"verify failed\"` / `\"new test failures: {newFailures}\"` \u2192 `\"verify failed [check:red treeHash:{hash}]\"` / `\"new test failures: {newFailures} [check:red treeHash:{hash}]\"`\n2. `VerifyFix.cs:220-221` \u2014 fix-verify exhaustion: change `\"verify failed after N fix-verify attempts\"` \u2192 `\"verify failed after N fix-verify attempts [check:red treeHash:{hash}]\"`\n3. `VerifyFix.cs:107-108,128-130,150-152,168-170` \u2014 other verify-time hard failures: append `[check:red treeHash:{hash}]` to existing reason strings\n\nThe `{hash}` would be the `treeHash` already computed in `VerifyObservability.cs:38` (passed through to the call site via `failingTestOutput` path or recomputed).\n\n*Pros:* Minimal surface-area change, no new types or schemas, the signature lands directly in `FlagReason` and flows through all existing consumers.  \n*Cons:* String-formatted data is fragile if consumers need to parse it programmatically; the hash must be available at each flag call site (already is for most).\n\n### Option B \u2014 Add a structured `VerifySignature` field to `FailedRunContext`\n\nAdd a new record type `VerifySignature(string Check, string TreeHash, int? ExitCode, string? FailureReason)` and a new nullable field on `FailedRunContext`. Write the signature to a small JSON file (e.g., `verify-signature.json`) alongside `NEEDS-REVIEW` in `FlagAsync` (or after `PublishVerifyResultAsync`). Have `FailedRunContextReader.Read` parse it. `FixTaskAuthorRunner.BuildPrompt` then emits it as a dedicated section.\n\n*Pros:* Structured, machine-parseable, doesn't overload the human-readable `FlagReason` string.  \n*Cons:* Larger change \u2014 new file write, new type, new parsing logic, new prompt section; extra filesystem I/O on every flag.\n\n### Option C \u2014 Enrich the `NEEDS-REVIEW` file with a `verify-signature:` header line\n\nAfter the `reason` line and `stage N` line, add a third metadata line like `verify-signature: red <treeHash>` in the `FlagAsync` method (only when the caller supplies verify signature info). Have `FailedRunContextReader` recognize this line and expose it as a new property.\n\n*Pros:* Single-file, minimal new surface, backward-compatible (old `NEEDS-REVIEW` files without the line produce null).  \n*Cons:* Still a free-text convention that needs regex parsing; more consumers must be updated if the field is ever depended on programmatically.\n\n---\n\n```json\n{ \"summary\": \"Carry the verify check result, tree hash, and failure reason (the 'verify signature') into the FlagReason string so fix-task authoring has immediate access to the condensed verify summary without separate output-file parsing.\", \"options\": [\"Option A \u2014 Embed compact verify signature [check:red treeHash:<hash>] in the FlagReason string at the three verify-flag call sites\", \"Option B \u2014 Add a structured VerifySignature record type and field on FailedRunContext, persisted as verify-signature.json\", \"Option C \u2014 Add a verify-signature: metadata line to the NEEDS-REVIEW file and expose it via FailedRunContextReader\"] }\n```",
    "exit_code": 0
  },
